    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our premier efficiency score of 81.88. His massive matchup against Miles Mikolas, coupled with a projected leadoff spot and dynamic platoon advantage, creates an ideal environment for elite production. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Josh Lowe** (71.68) follow closely as primary catalysts; **Josh Lowe** is particularly well-positioned to capitalize on Roki Sasaki\u2019s high xERA of 5.23, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from the same favorable matchup against Brandon Young that elevates **Nasim Nunez** (65.25) and **Brady House** (63.19). We are banking on this collective exposure to Brandon Young to anchor our offensive floor, as the lineup's collective ability to exploit that specific pitching vulnerability is the primary driver of today's scoring projection.\n\nThe decision to exclude **Andy Pages** from the active roster was the day\u2019s most difficult call. His score of 56.26 barely missed the cut behind the more stable situational output of **Dominic Smith** and **Sam Antonacci**. While **Andy Pages** remains a high-upside asset, the optimizer prioritized the specific platoon advantages of **Dominic Smith** and the elite 0.400 xwOBA profile of **Sam Antonacci**, despite the minor wind-in risk affecting the latter. We are proceeding with caution regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Nolan Schanuel**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Brady House**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Josh Lowe**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Sam Antonacci**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**; should any of these hitters shift down in their respective orders, we will reassess our game-cap exposure. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (62.75) faces a respectable test in Flaherty, his current scoring trajectory remains solid enough to warrant a start despite the slight dip from his base projection.",
